-- title:
--   Descent of the mathcal O_D-action along invariant coordinates
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a commutative Noetherian ring $B$, and write $B[\![x]\!]$ for $2$-variable power series over $B$. Let $X$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $B$ in the sense of `FormalODModule`: a $2$-dimensional formal group law $X.F$ that is commutative, a family of $2$-tuples of series $X.\mathrm{act}\,a$ indexed by $a$ in $\mathbb Z_{p^2}=W(\mathbb F_{p^2})$ and a $2$-tuple $X.\varpi$, each a law endomorphism of $X.F$ (zero constant terms and compatible with $X.F$), with $X.\mathrm{act}\,1$ the identity, $X.\mathrm{act}(ab)$ the composite of $X.\mathrm{act}\,a$ and $X.\mathrm{act}\,b$, $X.\mathrm{act}(a+b)$ the $X.F$-sum of the two, $X.\varpi\circ X.\varpi=X.\mathrm{act}\,p$ and $X.\varpi\circ X.\mathrm{act}\,a=X.\mathrm{act}(\sigma a)\circ X.\varpi$ for the Witt vector Frobenius $\sigma$. Let $I\subseteq B[\![x]\!]$ be an ideal whose quotient $B[\![x]\!]/I$ is finite and projective over $B$, and which is stable under substitution of $X.\mathrm{act}\,a$ for every $a$ and of $X.\varpi$. Let $u=(u_1,u_2)$ be a $2$-tuple of series with zero constant terms which is invariant in the sense that for each $j$ the difference $u_j(X.F(x,y))-u_j(x)$ lies in the ideal generated by $I$ in the variables $y$, and which satisfies the parametric descent property: for every $n$ and every $w\in B[\![x,t_1,\dots,t_n]\!]$ with $w(X.F(x,y),t)-w(x,t)$ in the ideal generated by $I$ in the variables $y$, there is a unique $W$ with $W(u(x),t)=w(x,t)$. Finally let $G$ be a commutative $2$-dimensional formal group law over $B$ for which $u$ is a homomorphism of laws $X.F\to G$, i.e. $u_i(X.F(x,y))=G(u(x),u(y))_i$ for all $i$. Then there exists a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $Y$ over $B$ with $Y.F=G$ such that $u$ is $\mathcal O_D$-linear from $X$ to $Y$: $u$ is a homomorphism of laws $X.F\to Y.F$, $u\circ X.\mathrm{act}\,a=Y.\mathrm{act}\,a\circ u$ for every $a\in\mathbb Z_{p^2}$, and $u\circ X.\varpi=Y.\varpi\circ u$. Only existence of such a $Y$ is asserted, not its uniqueness.
--
--   This is the step in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd uniformisation material which transports the $\mathcal O_D$-module structure from $X$ to the quotient law $G$ obtained by dividing by the finite subgroup cut out by $I$, the $\mathcal O_D$-stability of $I$ being what makes the action descend along the invariant coordinates $u$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_isIsogenyOfHeight_of_invariant_coordinates`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.FormalODModule.exists_isIsogenyOfHeight_of_invariant_coordinates), which packages the resulting map $u : X \to Y$ as an isogeny of prescribed height.
-- source:
